  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Gary Burke began his career with a Lloyd's broker, arranging insurance for art, jewellery and valuable homes. Those specialist risks gave him a foundation for a business aimed at regional brokers. He helped them obtain cover from mainstream insurers through an expanding panel, widening their options beyond Lloyd's.\n\nThe next problem he tackled was access to technology for small-business insurance. His team built an online system that let brokers compare prices from several underwriters immediately. Brokers could offer the same comparison service through their own branded websites, while specialist staff handled underwriting decisions. The approach combined a digital distribution tool with experienced insurance support.",
